# APML Interface: Listening MODE — Dialogue surface
# SSI Learning App
# Version: 1.2.0
# Last updated: 2026-08-06
# Source: packages/player-vue/src/components/ListeningOverlay.vue
#         packages/player-vue/src/composables/useListeningPods.ts
#         packages/player-vue/src/components/SettingsScreen.vue (entry point)

## ============================================================================
## OVERVIEW
## ============================================================================

SPECIFICATION:
  name: "Listening MODE — Dialogues"
  purpose: |
    A standalone PRACTICE surface where the learner replays the course's
    listening-pod dialogues (Layer 2 content) on demand. Distinct from the
    MAIN FLOW, where the same pod content is delivered through the staged
    9-stage acquisition progression (usePodLapScheduler, driven live from
    algorithm_config.pods).
  principle: |
    Listening MODE is for PRACTICE, not acquisition. The structured staged
    delivery lives ONCE, in the main flow. This surface does NOT re-implement
    a summarised copy of it — a second, drifting engine was the root cause of
    the listening-vs-main-flow mismatch (Tom, 2026-06-12). The two learner
    modes here are deliberately simple and TARGET-ONLY.

## ============================================================================
## ENTRY POINT
## ============================================================================

ENTRY_POINT:
  where: "Settings → Tools → 'Listening mode' (SettingsScreen.vue)"
  flow: |
    SettingsScreen emits 'openListening' → PlayerContainer closes settings and
    calls LearningPlayer.handleListeningToggle() → showListeningOverlay = true.
    Leaving is unchanged: the transport's back/play button (BottomNav
    exitListeningMode) closes the overlay and stops audio.
  not_in_the_player_flow: |
    The mode popup (ModeTray) no longer offers listening. Aran, 2026-08-06:
    "don't think the 'listening mode' popup is a good idea, it was distracting,
    I think it's okay for it to live under the settings". So the tray's
    "Mode — pick one" radio group (HISE / Listening) and its
    selectExperienceMode handler are gone; the tray keeps Pronunciation guide
    and Offline. (Turbo was in that list too until it was RETIRED 2026-08-06;
    the two learner-facing modes are now easy/fast, chosen from a segmented
    control on the player's resting screen, not from the tray.) HISE is simply
    what the player does when no mode is on.
  copy_kept_for_reuse: |
    The tray copy stays in the locales as modes.listening / modes.listeningDesc
    ("Listening" / "Audio only, no speaking"), unused for now.
  in_flow_ruling: |
    Tom, 2026-08-06, settling the messaging question Aran raised: a listening
    exercise goes STRAIGHT IN with the audio, introduced by the spoken "now
    just listen for a while" — no popup, no modal, nothing persistent, because
    the screen is needed for the displayed text. The pod-start reminder
    transient is deleted (see learning-player.apml v2.1.25). The preparation
    guidance survives where it does not interrupt: the learner explainer's
    "What the listening stretches ask of you", and this settings entry.
  locale_keys: |
    The settings row uses the already-translated settings.listeningMode /
    settings.listeningModeDesc.

## ============================================================================
## TABS
## ============================================================================

TABS:
  dialogues:
    key: "pods"
    label: "Dialogues"
    content: "Listening-pod scenes for the course (useListeningPods)."
    flow: |
      Scene list → tap a scene → teleprompter plays the scene through.
      On scene end: advance to the next scene (continuous), unless the
      loop toggle is on (repeat current scene, Spotify single-track style).
  core:
    key: "seeds"
    label: "Core"
    content: "Seed sentences. Has the speed selector (1× / 1.2× / 1.5× / 2×)."
  all:
    key: "phrases"
    label: "All"
    content: "Every practice phrase. Has the speed selector."

## ============================================================================
## DIALOGUE MODES (the difficulty/practice selector, scene view only)
## ============================================================================

DIALOGUE_MODES:
  description: |
    Immersion/Drill selector shown on every PLAYBACK surface: Dialogues with a
    scene open AND Core (seeds) (Aran 2026-06-29 — Core gets the modes too; the
    gating computed is `modeSurface = isDialogueScene || view==='seeds'`). "All"
    (phrases) stays the legacy random-voice list. Keys are stable (localStorage
    'ssi-listening-mode' + code); a retired/unknown stored key migrates to the
    default (immersion).

    Rows are ONE PER CHUNK (per-phrase granularity) — openScene flattens the
    scene's turns into a row per listening_pod_sentences chunk. The turn
    grouping survives only as presentation: the speaker chip shows on a turn's
    FIRST chunk, and the inter-row gap is turn-aware. Because a row is a single
    phrase, the known-language gloss is a single line under it (never a
    paragraph wall) and follows the gloss eye in EVERY mode — target-first by
    leaving the eye where the learner sets it.

  immersion:
    key: "immersion"
    label: "Immersion"
    default: true
    desc: "The whole scene in the target language, at your pace."
    audio: |
      Each unit's TARGET played once at the learner's chosen speed. Within a
      speaker's turn chunks run tight (50ms) for natural continuous speech; a
      speaker change / between-row gap is ~90ms (Aran 2026-06-29: all gaps ≤0.1s).
    speed_row: true   # interactive 1×/1.2×/1.5×/2× selector

  drill:
    key: "drill"
    label: "Drill"
    desc: "Hear the meaning, then drill the line — normal, then twice fast."
    audio: |
      Per unit: the KNOWN (English) clip ONCE (hear the meaning), then the
      TARGET ×3 at base · 2×base · 2×base, where base = the chosen speed (Aran
      2026-06-29). So speed 1× → 1/2/2; speed 1.2× → 1.2/2.4/2.4. The English
      clip is `knownAudioId` (per-sentence when the turn was split, else the
      turn-level clip; Core uses the seed's own known_audio_id); it is skipped
      when a unit has no known clip (the target reps still play). ~90ms gaps.
    speed_row: true   # the speed selector is now EXPOSED in Drill (the chosen
                      # speed is the "normal" rate; the fixed-pace caption/spacer
                      # is retired).
    slice_playback: |
      DISABLED (2026-07-10). Sub-sentence ms-slice playback of Take G is off
      via DRILL_SLICE_PLAYBACK_ENABLED=false in @ssi/core pods/fusionDrill.ts:
      the seam diagnosis found ~35% of ita groups with misplaced seams (ffmpeg
      silence-detect fallback picks wrong gaps), and a bad split is worse than
      no split (Tom). Every fusion group self-clamps to its whole: Drill shows
      one text strip per sentence and plays the natural sentence take; the
      main-flow unified ladder likewise enters at Stage 1. Text chunking,
      glosses and window knowns stay authored and intact. Flip the const back
      when per-chunk rendered clips land.

  audit:
    key: "audit"
    label: "Progression"
    status: "ADMIN-ONLY (implemented)"
    visibility: |
      Gated by isSsiAdmin AND the Settings → Developer "Listening Progression
      Audit" toggle (localStorage 'ssi-listening-audit'). The overlay appends
      the mode to LISTEN_MODES only when both hold; flipping the toggle is
      picked up live via the 'ssi-setting-changed' window event. If audit is
      selected and then becomes unavailable, the selection falls back to
      immersion.
    desc: |
      The REAL 9-stage acquisition progression, read live from
      algorithm_config.pods (the same config the main-flow scheduler uses),
      so it matches the main flow by construction and reflects Popty tweaks
      instantly. For each chunk, plays EVERY stage of the live config in order
      (stages 1→N), so the content team hears a line's whole arc in one pass.
      Role → audio + role → rate resolution reuse the scheduler's helpers
      (explainer falls back to translation; ROLE_SPEED from usePodLapScheduler).
      A live badge shows "Stage s/N · role · line c/N". This is the ONLY
      Dialogue mode that surfaces known-language audio/text, and the only one
      whose pace comes from the config rather than the learner.

## ============================================================================
## PLAYBACK MAPPING (ListeningOverlay.buildPlayQueue)
## ============================================================================

PLAYBACK:
  source_unit: |
    useListeningPods still merges consecutive same-speaker chunks into turns
    (for the conversation colouring + speaker chips), but openScene FLATTENS
    those turns into one row per chunk, tagging each row with speakerName (on
    the turn's first chunk only) and isTurnStart. Each row carries single-chunk
    `sentences` detail (targetAudioId / knownAudioId / explainerAudioId).
  unified_queue: |
    buildModalQueue(units) is shared by dialogue (units = a row's per-chunk
    sentences) and Core (units = the seed's own { targetAudioId, knownAudioId }).
    base = chosen speed. immersion → target once @base. drill → known once @base,
    then target @base · 2×base · 2×base. "All" (phrases) keeps the legacy
    random-voice queue (rate=null).
  inter_row_gap: |
    Tightened to ≤0.1s everywhere (Aran 2026-06-29). Constants:
    GAP_DEFAULT_MS=90 (Core/All between phrases + dialogue speaker-change, was
    800), GAP_DRILL_MS=90 (between Drill reps + Drill within-turn, was 300/350),
    GAP_IMMERSION_JOIN_MS=50 (same-speaker sentence join in Immersion, the only
    deliberately-tighter gap).
  rate_handling: |
    Modal queues (dialogue + Core) always carry an explicit per-clip rate, so a
    speed picked elsewhere never leaks. "All" passes rate=null and relies on the
    audio controller's playback-rate watch.
  warm_ahead: |
    Immersion warms TARGET clips ahead (lock-screen-safe); Drill ALSO warms the
    per-line KNOWN clip, since it now leads each line.

## ============================================================================
## TRANSPORT (Aran 2026-06-29)
## ============================================================================

TRANSPORT:
  persistent_play_stop: |
    A top-left play/stop transport-btn is now shown in EVERY view, including a
    dialogue scene (the old tap-anywhere-to-play / click-outside-to-stop was
    undiscoverable). Same togglePlayback behaviour everywhere.
  play_all_scenes: |
    The Dialogues scene-list has a "Play all scenes" button (playAllScenes):
    opens scene 1 and plays straight through — handleEndOfList already segues
    scene→scene (loop off), so the whole pod plays end-to-end as one session.

